# Security vs green CI

Anti-scraping is a **higher priority** than a green nightly. Do not suggest weakening it to stop false alarms.

## Never suggest

- Turning **Cloudflare Bot Fight Mode** (or JS Detections) off, pausing it for the nightly window, or allowing GitHub runner IPs, just so `prod-smoke-edge` passes
- Removing orange-cloud proxy, honeytokens, contact-reveal, or RLS on public directory views for the same reason

Bot Fight Mode was turned **on 2026-08-09** as P1 HTML-scrape friction after PostgREST dumps were closed. GitHub Actions IPs often get *Just a moment…*. That is expected.

## How to read Production Monitoring

| Edge (mydoccy.com) | Origin (`*.vercel.app`) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| Fail (*Just a moment…*) | Pass | Runners vs Bot Fight. **Do nothing.** Keep Bot Fight on. |
| Fail | Fail | Look at the **product** (origin). |
| Pass | Pass | All good. |

Fix **tests** (cookie bar, force-click, waits). Treat edge as diagnostic when origin is configured. Do not disable Cloudflare.
